From: Silicon Bakery (t6020 port) <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] t6020 (M2 Pro): SoC row, AXI2AF tunables, ADT DVAs, overlay variant 15

Against github.com/aquarat/apple-m-series-ave-driver
9ab14e45281e8f61fb499b760408028171a5f2b5 (apply with `git apply` or `patch -p1`).
Static port, written on the Mac14,9 itself under macOS; not compiled and
not run on hardware. See docs/ave-port.txt for the provenance of every value and the
bring-up plan.

- driver/ave_soc.[ch]: ave_soc_t6020 (H14S, DevID 19/16/11, Hera_6020 DPE
  set, t8110 DART, translated fetch, src_dims, no DAPF programming), and
  three row fields: axi2af_fw, iboot.ioba_unchecked, iboot.dva_from_adt.
- driver/ave_drv.c, ave.h: "apple,t6020-ave"; AVE_AXI2AF tunables applied
  after the DPE tunables (axi2af_tunables=, default 1), as macOS's
  AVE_HwC::PowerOn does on DevType 16-18.
- driver/ave_fw.c: rows with dva_from_adt take TEXT/DATA DVAs and the DATA
  literal from the live ADT's segment-ranges remap fields; the pristine
  check can skip IOBA.
- tools/ave_fwgen.py: Hera_6020 DPE set, `axi2af` subcommand, t6020 tags.
- test/: ave-overlay-t6020.dts as variant=15 (refused unless apple,t6020).
- tools/ave-load.sh: t6020 -> VARIANT=15.  dts/apple,ave.yaml: compatible.

---
